# Adding features in this Flutter template

This is a reusable app template (package `app_template`). Do not modify Vokey (`StudioProjects/vokey`). Use **flutter_bloc + GetIt**. Do not add Riverpod, Provider, or GetX.

## Layers

```
features → core → Flutter / SDKs
```

Features must not import other features. `core/` must not import `features/`.

```
lib/features/<name>/
  domain/        entities, repository interfaces, use cases (Either<Failure, T>)
  data/          models, datasources, repository impls
  presentation/  cubit/bloc + screens (BlocBuilder / context.read)
```

Shared widgets go in `lib/shared/`. Identity is `AppIdentity` / `project_config.yaml`. Secrets stay in gitignored `.env.dev` / `.env.prod`.

## Checklist for a new feature

1. Create the slice under `lib/features/<name>/` as above. Copy paywall as the shape (`features/paywall/`).
2. REST: add the path to `ApiRoutes`, a Retrofit `*ApiService`, and Freezed request/response DTOs. Register the service with `AppApiClient.dio`. Datasources use `_client.run(() => _api....)`. Do not hardcode hosts or call Dio directly.
3. Register implementations in `configureDependencies()` (`lib/core/di/injection.dart`). Screens take BLoC from `context.read` / `BlocProvider`; services from `getIt<T>()`.
4. Add `RoutePaths` + `GoRoute` in `lib/core/constants/route_paths.dart` and `lib/core/router/app_router.dart`. Use `RoutePaths.absolute` before `router.go` so paths like `paywall` do not nest.
5. Product flags: add a key + default in `RemoteConfigKeys` / `RemoteConfigDefaults` and `remoteconfig.template.json`, or `GrowthBookKeys` for experiments. Document it in `STARTUP.md`.
6. Tests next to existing ones under `test/`. Fake repositories/datasources; do not hit real Play/Firebase/network.
7. Dont make changes to existing auth, paywall, events unless exlicitly mentioned.
8. Make widgets child classes in seperate files dont make multiple classes in single class
9. If the change is architectural (new core module, new RC key, new API, new gated SDK), update `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `STARTUP.md`, and `CODEWALKTHROUGH.md`.

## Do

```dart
// ✅ domain use case returns Either
Future<Either<Failure, Plan>> call() => repository.fetchPlan(id);

// ✅ presentation
context.read<PaywallPlanCubit>().load();
getIt<AppUpdateService>().checkOnLaunch();
```

## Don't

```dart
// ❌ feature importing another feature
import 'package:app_template/features/auth/presentation/screens/auth_screen.dart';

// ❌ hardcoded product URL or Voice Club / Vokey-only API
dio.get('https://api.voiceclub.app/...');
```

Use package imports (`package:app_template/...`). Match existing naming (`*Cubit`, `<Interface>Impl` for the production implementation). Do not invent prefixes like `Rest*` / `Firebase*` when there is a single impl — `AuthRemoteDataSource` → `AuthRemoteDataSourceImpl`. Vendor-named classes are only for multiple interchangeable impls (`FirebaseAnalyticsService`, `MixpanelAnalyticsService`). Fakes stay `Fake*`. Paywall checkout is Capslock Payments (`CheckoutClient` + host-owned `PaywallCheckout` / `UpiService`); do not add a second billing SDK, pick Cashfree/PhonePe on the client, or depend on SDK `PaymentWidget` (removed). Truecaller is optional: when `AppConfig.hasTruecaller` and the platform is Android, auto-launch the sheet on the auth screen (once per visit) and keep the CTA as a retry; silence SDK unavailability / cancel so OTP stays available.
